. Long C, Tang S, Wang R, Ji L, Wang Y, Wu T, et al. The migrating mediators and the interaction associated with the use of essential public health services: a cross-sectional study in Chinese older migrants. BMC Geriatr. (2020) 20:475. 10.1186/s12877-020-01878-0 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 21. Zeng W, Wang C, Chen H, Tong B, Li D, Zou Z, et al. Health status and public health education for internal older migrants in China: evidence from a nationally representative survey. Front Public Health. (2022) 10:937361. 10.3389/fpubh.2022.937361 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 22. Wang XH, Li JB, Yang Y. Status and influencing factors of receiving health education and personal health record establishment among elderly migrant population in China. Chin J Public Health. (2021) 37:203–8. 10.11847/zgggws1128961 [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] 23. Xu X, Zhang Q, You H, Wu Q. Awareness, utilization and health outcomes of national essential public health service among migrants in China. Front Public Health. (2022) 10:936275. 10.3389/fpubh.2022.936275 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 24. Tang S, Long C, Wang R, Liu Q, Feng D, Feng Z. Improving the utilization of essential public health services by Chinese elderly migrants: strategies and policy implication. J Glob Health. (2020) 10:010807. 10.7189/jogh.10.010807 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 25. Cailhol J, Lombrail P. Towards equity in migrant''s health? Rev Prat. (2019) 69:668–9. [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 26. Fernández-Gutiérrez M, Bas-Sarmiento P, Albar-Marín MJ, Paloma-Castro O, Romero-Sánchez JM. Health literacy interventions for immigrant populations: a systematic review. Int Nurs Rev. (2018) 65:54–64. 10.1111/inr.12373 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 27. Bien B, McKee KJ, Döhner H, Triantafillou J, Lamura G, Doroszkiewicz H, et al. Disabled older people''s use of health and social care services and their unmet 