lutions. Prev Med. 2014;61:114–115. doi: 10.1016/j.ypmed.2014.01.011. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 16. Canadian Institutes of Health Research. Health Equity Matters—Institute of Population and Public Health Strategic Plan—2015–2018. Ottawa, Ontario: 2015. [ Google Scholar ] 17. Brownson RC, Fielding JE, Maylahn CM. Evidence-based public health: a fundamental concept for public health practice. Annu Rev Public Health. 2009;30:175–201. doi: 10.1146/annurev.publhealth.031308.100134. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 18. Wallerstein N, Duran B. Community-based participatory research contributions to intervention research: the intersection of science and practice to improve health equity. Am J Public Health. 2010;100(suppl 1):S40–S46. doi: 10.2105/AJPH.2009.184036. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 19. Quebec Population Health Research Network. Available at: http://www.santepop.qc.ca/en . Accessed June 20, 2016. 20. Canadian Institutes of Health Research. Strategic Training Initiative in Health Research (STIHR) 2001–2006: Final Evaluation Report. Ottawa, Ontario: 2008. [ Google Scholar ] 21. Weiss CH. Theory-based evaluation: past, present, and future. New Dir Eval. 1997;76:41–55. [ Google Scholar ] 22. Erwin PC, Barlow P, Brownson RC, Amos K, Keck CW. Characteristics of academic health departments: initial findings from a cross-sectional survey. J Public Health Manag Pract. 2016;22(2):190–193. doi: 10.1097/PHH.0000000000000237. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 23. Eidson M, Pradhan E, Morse D. Assessing the contributions of an academic health department for a school of public health in New York State. Public Health Rep. 2014;129(3):296–302. doi: 10.1177/003335491412900313. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 24. Jacobs JA, Duggan K, Erwin PC et al. Capacity building for evidence-based decision making in local health departments: scaling up an effective training approach. Implement Sci