J Manag World. (2008) 179:52–8. 10.19744/j.cnki.11-1235/f.2008.08.006 [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] 29. Kou ZL. Drug-based medical care” and “expensive and difficult to see doctor. J World Econ. (2010) 33:49–68. 10.19985/j.cnki.cassjwe.2010.01.004 [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] 30. Wang J. The economic impact of special economic zones: evidence from Chinese municipalities. J Develop Econ. (2013) 101:133–47. 10.1016/j.jdeveco.2012.10.009 [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] 31. Guo F, Xiong RX. Local financial institutions and regional economic growth: a quasi-natural experiment of city commercial banks in China. China Econ Quart. (2018) 17:221–46. 10.13821/j.cnki.ceq.2017.04.09 [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] 32. Sun M, Li XW. Air pollution and public health: An empirical study based on provincial panel data. Pop J. (2017) 39:5–13. 10.16405/j.cnki.1004-129X.2017.05.001 [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] 33. Jacobson LS, Lalonde RJ, Sullivan DG. Earingis losses if diplaced workers. Am Econom Rev. (1993) 84:685–709. [ Google Scholar ] 34. Guo B, Feng Y, Hu F. Have carbon emission trading pilot policy improved urban innovation capacity? Evidence from a quasi-natural experiment in China. Environ Sci Pollut Res. 3:5699. 10.1007/s11356-023-25699-x [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 35. Fan ZY, Tian BB. Tax competition, tax enforcement and tax avoidance. Econ Res J. (2013) 48:99–111. [ Google Scholar ] 36. Guo B, Wang Y, Feng Y, Liang C, Tang L, Yao X, Hu F. The effects of environmental tax reform on urban air pollution: a quasi-natural experiment based on the environmental protection tax law. Front Public Health. (2022) 10:7524. 10.3389/fpubh.2022.967524 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 37. Wen ZL, Zhang L. Testing and application of the mediating effects. Acta Psychologica Sinica. (2004) 05:614–20. [ Google Scholar ] 38. Chen R, Zheng YH. Mediating analysis: principles, procedures, bootstrap methods and applications. J Market Sci. (2013) 9:120–35. [ Google Scholar ] Assoc